    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know people say it's not permanent, but it feels so factual. like, if a glass breaks into a million tiny pieces, you can't just glue it back together and expect it to hold water again. i've been through so much that i feel like the pieces are just... gone. it's exhausting trying to pretend there's something to fix when there's just nothing left.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That analogy of the broken glass is a really powerful way to describe how deeply you are hurting right now. It makes complete sense that you feel exhausted when the effort to \"fix\" feels pointless if the core seems shattered. Instead of viewing it as something to be perfectly *repaired*, perhaps the focus could be on gently tending to the fragments, however small they are. A therapist can help you explore ways to find strength and meaning within the pieces you still have.",
      "source": "target",
